** {color:#36b37e}If this is not updated or full, we should migrate each user{color}

!image-20261028-174744.png|width=760,alt="image-20261028-174744.png"!

!image-20261028-174946.png|width=760,alt="image-20261028-174946.png"!



*US-R9.1 See Debt transactions in CaseTrack.* As an attorney, I want a client's transactions from Forth to appear in CaseTrack, so that I can check payments without opening Forth.

* Payments and fees appear on the client record with date, type, amount and status.
* New transactions appear within a few minutes of being recorded in Forth. {color:#36b37e}(This payments are automatically running everyday at certain hour){color}
* Amounts show in dollars with two decimals.

*US-R9.2 Trust the numbers.* As an administrator, I want a reconciliation check between the two systems, so that missing or wrong transactions are found quickly.

* A report compares transaction counts and totals per client between CaseTrack and Forth.
* Differences are listed with the affected client and date range.
* A sync failure raises an alert to administrators.

*US-R9.3 No duplicate or lost transactions.* As an administrator, I want each transaction to sync exactly once, so that totals are never inflated or short.

* Re-running a sync does not create duplicates.
* A voided or changed transaction in Forth is reflected in CaseTrack.
